content.text:
Now mobile library fixed and more usable, but the "Índice compartido" card is huge (95px tall) and only 2 lines. Could reduce padding/height. It's a block spanning 2 cols; 11px padding + content maybe fine. It has v0.8 plus text. Could align horizontal: at mobile, `.lib-storage{display:flex;flex-direction:row;align-items:center;gap:10px}` and small margin. But not critical. Yet screenshot indicates the card has big empty space below text (95px height). Because flex justify-content center and maybe height? `.library-stats .lib-storage` inherits grid row height? It spans but no fixed height. 95 suggests content 3 lines + padding 22 = maybe 54; 95 maybe because other grid cells? Wait all grid rows: row1 2 items ~72px, row2 2 items ~72, row3 storage 95. It might be stretched? CSS `.library-stats>div{padding:11px 13px;border-bottom...}`; lib-storage padding. Height 95 likely due align-items stretch to a row with min? Hmm. Could set `.library-stats .lib-storage{padding-top:9px;padding-bottom:9px}` and `small` line. Not a major issue; but visually empty. We can restructure it as horizontal at mobile:
```
@media(max-width:900){.library-stats .lib-storage{flex-direction:row;align-items:center;gap:12px;justify-content:flex-start}}
.library-stats .lib-storage b{order:1}
.library-stats .lib-storage span{...}
```
But `.lib-storage` includes `<span>ÍNDICE COMPARTIDO</span><b>v0.8</b><small>...`; flex row would place all 3 inline. That could look nice: "ÍNDICE COMPARTIDO  v0.8   28 de 28 ubicaciones verificadas". Let's do at mobile:
```
.library-stats .lib-storage{display:flex;flex-direction:row;align-items:center;gap:8px}
.library-stats .lib-storage span{margin:0}
.library-stats .lib-storage small{margin:0;margin-left:auto;font-size:7px}
```
But the spans inside small also matched by `.library-stats>div span`? We override. Fine.
At desktop keep column? Desktop card width ~? It looked okay. Could also make it horizontal desktop to avoid empty. Let's do universally: `.lib-storage` row with wrap? At desktop rightmost col width ~1.5fr (~260px) enough for "ÍNDICE COMPARTIDO" + v0.8 + text maybe wraps. Use:
```
.library-stats .lib-storage{display:flex;flex-direction:row;align-items:center;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.library-stats .lib-storage b{font-size:11px}
.library-stats .lib-storage small{flex-basis:100%;margin-top:0}
```
This reduces height. But on mobile, text under. Fine. Yet not vital.

More important: the toolbar now has 3 rows (search, selects, sort, toggle) which takes lots vertical space. It's okay on mobile; still above fold list starts at 700. Fine.

Need check mobile process with bottom nav not interrupted. Good.

Now recheck desktop library after CSS fix maybe. Resize 1280; screenshot maybe not necessary. But need ensure toolbar fits. Let's do final panel and maybe library.

